---
/**
 * Where a subscriber goes after paying.
 *
 * There is nothing to paste any more. Premium is an account: you sign in inside
 * the app with a code sent to your email, and it stays premium through renewals
 * without you doing anything. So this section's job is only to say where to go
 * and what to expect — the sign-in itself happens in the app, because that is
 * the thing that needs to know.
 */
---

<section class="wrap section" id="signin">
  <div class="section-label">Already subscribed?</div>
  <p class="lead">
    Premium is tied to your account, not to a key you have to keep. Open the app,
    go to <strong>Settings → Subscription</strong>, and sign in with the email
    address you subscribed with. We'll send you a six-digit code — there's no
    password to remember.
  </p>

  <ul class="list-plain" style="margin-top: var(--space-4); max-width: 62ch">
    <li>Renewals need nothing from you — the app checks your subscription itself.</li>
    <li>Works offline. It only needs to reach us occasionally to stay current.</li>
    <li>
      Cancel any time and premium keeps working to the end of the period you
      already paid for.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="footnote">
    Signing in on a new machine is the same three steps, and you can be signed in
    on as many as you like. Signing out on one doesn't affect the others.
  </p>
</section>
